343
00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:26.950
you warm up for 5 or 10 minutes,

344
00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:29.984
and then you start at a certain wattage,

345
00:13:29.984 --> 00:13:32.090
I think, if memory serves me,

346
00:13:32.090 --> 00:13:35.630
we started at something really easy like 100 watts,

347
00:13:35.630 --> 00:13:39.470
and every four minutes you increase the wattage 10 watts

348
00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:41.620
and you prick, you have your finger pricked

349
00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:45.740
for blood lactate, you calculate your heart rate

350
00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:50.140
at that interval point and you give your perceived effort,

351
00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:52.460
like how hard is this on a scale of 1 to 10,

352
00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:55.740
and then you just keep increasing the wattage until failure

353
00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:59.060
and then you plot those metrics on a graph.

354
00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:02.450
And you can see when you get this crazy uptick

355
00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:05.330
is where you're going from your anaerobic energy system

356
00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:07.510
to your anaerobic energy system.

357
00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:11.940
And true endurance is reflected when that upward tick

358
00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:16.430
is way down the line in terms of wattage.

359
00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:18.210
And instead of like a hockey stick,

360
00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:20.520
it's a more gradual curve upwards.

361
00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:23.080
You're always trying to push that uptick out

362
00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:25.270
as far to the right as possible.

363
00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:26.330
And it's pretty revealing.

