2047
01:24:27.040 --> 01:24:28.700
and this is a little inside baseball,

2048
01:24:28.700 --> 01:24:29.630
but I think it's interesting

2049
01:24:29.630 --> 01:24:30.820
and I think people who read books

2050
01:24:30.820 --> 01:24:31.810
would find this interesting

2051
01:24:31.810 --> 01:24:33.550
if they're not already aware of it.

2052
01:24:33.550 --> 01:24:35.650
As I mentioned, like my book didn't make

2053
01:24:35.650 --> 01:24:37.230
the New York Times bestseller list,

2054
01:24:37.230 --> 01:24:40.000
it's had this low build, it continues to,

2055
01:24:40.000 --> 01:24:42.330
I mean, it's still like in top categories on Amazon,

2056
01:24:42.330 --> 01:24:43.580
particularly the audiobook--
That's amazing.

2057
01:24:43.580 --> 01:24:46.540
Like it's still number one, two, or three

2058
01:24:46.540 --> 01:24:49.450
in cycling, in running, in triathlon and stuff like that.

2059
01:24:49.450 --> 01:24:50.283
Amazing.

2060
01:24:50.283 --> 01:24:53.140
Which is great, but on the whole

2061
01:24:53.140 --> 01:24:55.270
like New York Times bestseller thing,

2062
01:24:55.270 --> 01:24:58.480
like I know from going through this process many times,

2063
01:24:58.480 --> 01:25:01.810
and also by dint of hosting authors

2064
01:25:01.810 --> 01:25:03.790
who have books coming out on the podcast

2065
01:25:03.790 --> 01:25:07.440
because now podcasting has become like a de rigeur stop

2066
01:25:07.440 --> 01:25:09.120
on the book publishing tour.

2067
01:25:09.120 --> 01:25:11.050
Like you have to go on these shows

2068
01:25:11.050 --> 01:25:12.870
and then we try to work with authors

2069
01:25:12.870 --> 01:25:16.650
so that the episodes come out around the book's release.

2070
01:25:16.650 --> 01:25:17.710
And I do the best I can.

2071
01:25:17.710 --> 01:25:19.040
I can't always commit to that.

2072
01:25:19.040 --> 01:25:21.310
But I understand that they're here

2073
01:25:22.600 --> 01:25:24.280
to try to get their book out into the world

2074
01:25:24.280 --> 01:25:27.268
and I certainly don't begrudge anyone that--

2075
01:25:27.268 --> 01:25:28.680
Like I'd be doing exactly the same thing.

2076
01:25:28.680 --> 01:25:32.900
So the way it works is there's a pre-order period

2077
01:25:32.900 --> 01:25:35.790
and then there's the publishing week.

2078
01:25:35.790 --> 01:25:39.470
And all book orders during that pre-order period

2079
01:25:39.470 --> 01:25:42.190
and including that first week after publication

2080
01:25:42.190 --> 01:25:44.450
all books come out on Tuesday, for some weird reason--

2081
01:25:44.450 --> 01:25:46.030
Right.

2082
01:25:46.030 --> 01:25:49.540
Are counted towards first week sales.

2083
01:25:49.540 --> 01:25:52.080
And that first week sales number

2084
01:25:52.080 --> 01:25:54.170
is what gets fed to the New York Times

2085
01:25:54.170 --> 01:25:57.020
and has a lot to do with how they crunch the numbers

2086
01:25:57.020 --> 01:26:01.300
and decide who makes that, who makes it on to the list.

2087
01:26:01.300 --> 01:26:04.010
What people don't know is that this system

2088
01:26:04.010 --> 01:26:06.020
is very easily gained.

2089
01:26:06.020 --> 01:26:08.240
Like you can literally buy your way

2090
01:26:08.240 --> 01:26:10.230
on to the New York Times bestseller list,

2091
01:26:10.230 --> 01:26:11.570
and many, many people do it.

2092
01:26:11.570 --> 01:26:13.520
I don't know, I know that like now

2093
01:26:13.520 --> 01:26:14.850
people are more aware of this

2094
01:26:14.850 --> 01:26:17.420
and perhaps the New York Times and other people

2095
01:26:17.420 --> 01:26:20.570
that compile these lists have precautionary members

2096
01:26:20.570 --> 01:26:25.440
to weed out bad actors, but at least the last time,

2097
01:26:25.440 --> 01:26:26.810
or when "Finding Ultra" came out,

2098
01:26:26.810 --> 01:26:28.210
like there's, there's like companies

2099
01:26:28.210 --> 01:26:29.900
that you can cut them a big check

2100
01:26:31.190 --> 01:26:33.760
and then they go and purchase the book

2101
01:26:33.760 --> 01:26:35.320
through all the varying outlets

2102
01:26:35.320 --> 01:26:37.350
at specified periods of time.

2103
01:26:37.350 --> 01:26:39.030
So they take your money and they use it

2104
01:26:39.030 --> 01:26:40.850
to buy your own book.

2105
01:26:40.850 --> 01:26:44.900
And the way it works is you can't just bum-rush Amazon

2106
01:26:44.900 --> 01:26:45.880
and buy a ton of books.

2107
01:26:45.880 --> 01:26:46.990
Like you gotta spread it out

2108
01:26:46.990 --> 01:26:50.180
through all the different online retailers, et cetera

2109
01:26:50.180 --> 01:26:53.023
so that it doesn't look like there's a bad actor.

2110
01:26:54.003 --> 01:26:55.520
There are people that know how to do these.

2111
01:26:55.520 --> 01:26:57.010
Do you burn your own book?

2112
01:26:57.010 --> 01:26:58.968
I don't know.
Who gets the books?

2113
01:26:58.968 --> 01:26:59.801
I mean, I can't imagine doing this,

2114
01:26:59.801 --> 01:27:04.120
but a lot of people do this so that they have huge numbers

2115
01:27:04.120 --> 01:27:07.010
during that pre-order period and during first week

2116
01:27:07.010 --> 01:27:09.270
and then they end up on the bestseller list.

2117
01:27:09.270 --> 01:27:13.189
But it's a complete, it's like fake news, right?

2118
01:27:13.189 --> 01:27:14.201
Right, right, right.

2119
01:27:14.201 --> 01:27:15.034
Like they've just bought their own book

2120
01:27:15.034 --> 01:27:16.650
and so their book disappears the following week,

2121
01:27:16.650 --> 01:27:18.830
no one's ever heard of it again.

2122
01:27:18.830 --> 01:27:22.270
At the same time, like I know a lot of CEOs

2123
01:27:22.270 --> 01:27:25.170
or high-net-worth people that put out books particularly

2124
01:27:25.170 --> 01:27:28.130
like business books or how-to books.

2125
01:27:28.130 --> 01:27:31.010
They can, because they're high-net-worth people,

2126
01:27:31.010 --> 01:27:32.610
can just buy their own book

2127
01:27:32.610 --> 01:27:35.370
and then like either give it to their staff

2128
01:27:35.370 --> 01:27:39.540
or resell the book when they do public speaking appearances.

2129
01:27:39.540 --> 01:27:41.520
So they're like, they double dip on it

2130
01:27:41.520 --> 01:27:43.950
but they buy a gigantic stash that they sit on

2131
01:27:43.950 --> 01:27:45.510
and can kind of sell over time

2132
01:27:45.510 --> 01:27:47.650
and that has the similar effect.

2133
01:27:47.650 --> 01:27:48.850
Interesting.
So it's crazy.

2134
01:27:48.850 --> 01:27:52.040
So that's why you'll see a book appear

2135
01:27:52.040 --> 01:27:54.920
and then you'll never hear about that book ever again.

2136
01:27:54.920 --> 01:27:56.667
That's a pretty good indication that,

2137
01:27:56.667 --> 01:27:59.540
and I would imagine that the New York Times

2138
01:27:59.540 --> 01:28:02.200
is probably much better at trying to figure out

2139
01:28:02.200 --> 01:28:03.590
who's doing this and who isn't.

2140
01:28:03.590 --> 01:28:06.470
Yeah. Also, I think, I'm pretty sure I don't have,

2141
01:28:06.470 --> 01:28:09.480
I don't know for a fact, but I'm pretty,

2142
01:28:09.480 --> 01:28:12.530
almost positive that also the New York Times

2143
01:28:12.530 --> 01:28:15.190
doesn't have like, it's not just about who sold the most,

2144
01:28:15.190 --> 01:28:16.750
they have like certain criteria,

2145
01:28:16.750 --> 01:28:18.455
like they're skewed against--

2146
01:28:18.455 --> 01:28:20.570
There is a weird subjectivity that gets injected to that.

2147
01:28:20.570 --> 01:28:21.710
Yeah, and I don't know what it is.

2148
01:28:21.710 --> 01:28:24.582
But like it's not really just straight who sold.

2149
01:28:24.582 --> 01:28:25.609
Not exactly.

2150
01:28:25.609 --> 01:28:26.980
It's not pure numbers.
Right.

2151
01:28:26.980 --> 01:28:29.480
And also, what is the current status

2152
01:28:29.480 --> 01:28:33.250
or their stance on self-published books, Adam?

2153
01:28:33.250 --> 01:28:34.140
Right. Well, they,

2154
01:28:34.140 --> 01:28:35.970
I mean, I don't think "Can't Hurt Me"

2155
01:28:35.970 --> 01:28:38.570
got a fair shake on that list at all.

2156
01:28:38.570 --> 01:28:39.950
Like it was--
So they did it,

2157
01:28:39.950 --> 01:28:41.900
was it ever on the list?
It was.

2158
01:28:41.900 --> 01:28:44.221
It was on the list, but it was like--

2159
01:28:44.221 --> 01:28:45.500
Interesting.

2160
01:28:45.500 --> 01:28:47.556
I thought that it wasn't--
So they have an audio list

2161
01:28:47.556 --> 01:28:48.420
and it was never on the audio list

2162
01:28:48.420 --> 01:28:50.320
even though we were,

2163
01:28:50.320 --> 01:28:55.040
we're still getting like one of the top

2164
01:28:55.040 --> 01:28:56.893
listened to audiobook still.

2165
01:28:58.220 --> 01:29:00.710
Audible's the main platform and we were, at the time,

2166
01:29:00.710 --> 01:29:02.330
like number two for months.

2167
01:29:02.330 --> 01:29:03.440
It was like you and--

2168
01:29:03.440 --> 01:29:05.010
And Michelle Obama.
Michelle Obama.

2169
01:29:05.010 --> 01:29:08.370
And then so I don't think we got a fair shake there.

2170
01:29:08.370 --> 01:29:10.380
It was on the general list maybe once

2171
01:29:10.380 --> 01:29:13.010
and then it was on the self-help list.

2172
01:29:13.010 --> 01:29:15.200
And so it was nice to be on the list and be recognized,

2173
01:29:15.200 --> 01:29:16.900
but it wasn't a fair shake because,

2174
01:29:16.900 --> 01:29:18.690
and I don't think it was reflective of the sales.

2175
01:29:18.690 --> 01:29:19.940
Yeah.
Yep.

2176
01:29:19.940 --> 01:29:21.570
Yeah, it's interesting how that works.

2177
01:29:21.570 --> 01:29:24.050
I mean, 'cause I just remember when it first came out.

2178
01:29:24.050 --> 01:29:25.777
I mean, obviously like it was selling like crazy

2179
01:29:25.777 --> 01:29:27.220
and it wasn't on the list.

2180
01:29:27.220 --> 01:29:28.235
Still, yeah.

2181
01:29:28.235 --> 01:29:30.460
But I believed at that time they had a policy

2182
01:29:30.460 --> 01:29:32.810
that self-published books were not eligible.

2183
01:29:32.810 --> 01:29:34.290
Exactly, and maybe that's over

2184
01:29:34.290 --> 01:29:36.650
because they're starting to cover self-published books

2185
01:29:36.650 --> 01:29:37.910
a little bit differently.

2186
01:29:37.910 --> 01:29:41.340
But like, what I loved about your thread was,

2187
01:29:41.340 --> 01:29:42.590
and talking about the long game,

2188
01:29:42.590 --> 01:29:44.250
is it ultimately doesn't matter

2189
01:29:44.250 --> 01:29:45.590
because what mattered more

2190
01:29:45.590 --> 01:29:47.770
is like what you're building towards.

2191
01:29:47.770 --> 01:29:50.340
And you said it yourself on your thread

2192
01:29:50.340 --> 01:29:53.820
that looking back that, that vanity phase,

2193
01:29:53.820 --> 01:29:56.520
doesn't even matter when you're talking about actually

2194
01:29:57.370 --> 01:29:59.670
influencing people and having people read it

2195
01:29:59.670 --> 01:30:01.970
and enjoying the book.

2196
01:30:01.970 --> 01:30:03.760
Yeah. I mean, I'm really proud of the fact

2197
01:30:03.760 --> 01:30:07.130
that it has become a perennial seller.

2198
01:30:07.130 --> 01:30:08.760
And that's very meaningful.

2199
01:30:08.760 --> 01:30:11.890
Like, "Who's buying your book 10 years later?"

2200
01:30:11.890 --> 01:30:16.160
seems like a more important metric, but less sexy

2201
01:30:16.160 --> 01:30:18.230
because I can't call myself a New York Times bestseller--

2202
01:30:18.230 --> 01:30:20.813
It's very uncommon, though, 10 years later, very.

2203
01:30:22.510 --> 01:30:26.070
Is there anything you would do differently, looking back,

2204
01:30:26.070 --> 01:30:29.250
in terms of what you included in the book,

2205
01:30:29.250 --> 01:30:30.903
any passages that stand out or things that--

2206
01:30:30.903 --> 01:30:32.060
I mean, 100%.

2207
01:30:32.060 --> 01:30:34.640
I don't think that you've grown as a human being

2208
01:30:34.640 --> 01:30:37.760
if you can look back on a creative work

2209
01:30:37.760 --> 01:30:39.540
and be satisfied with it.

2210
01:30:39.540 --> 01:30:40.740
I mean, I'm proud of it,

2211
01:30:42.402 --> 01:30:44.470
and I'm not about to like rewrite it again,

2212
01:30:44.470 --> 01:30:47.510
but, and I don't go back and crack it

2213
01:30:47.510 --> 01:30:49.977
'cause there's a certain cringe factor with that like--

2214
01:30:49.977 --> 01:30:51.854
You can't be seen doing that.

2215
01:30:51.854 --> 01:30:53.110
I don't listen to my own podcast.

2216
01:30:53.110 --> 01:30:54.780
You can't have your children running to you

2217
01:30:54.780 --> 01:30:56.910
reading your own book.
Yeah, no.

2218
01:30:56.910 --> 01:30:57.900
I mean, look, I don't need to.

2219
01:30:57.900 --> 01:31:01.090
But yeah, there's tons of stuff that I would change.

2220
01:31:01.090 --> 01:31:02.820
I think as you grow and you mature

2221
01:31:02.820 --> 01:31:05.680
and also you get a sense of like

2222
01:31:05.680 --> 01:31:08.660
what was important about that or meaningful and what wasn't.

2223
01:31:08.660 --> 01:31:11.780
And I had an opportunity to comb through it

2224
01:31:11.780 --> 01:31:13.187
a couple years ago when I rewrote it

2225
01:31:13.187 --> 01:31:14.760
and I took out a ton of stuff

2226
01:31:14.760 --> 01:31:15.593
that I couldn't even believe

2227
01:31:15.593 --> 01:31:17.330
that I included the first time around.

2228
01:31:17.330 --> 01:31:20.270
And I think today, if I was to go back and rewrite it,

2229
01:31:20.270 --> 01:31:23.470
the main thing I would do would be to just make it

2230
01:31:23.470 --> 01:31:26.510
a pure memoir and get rid of all the appendices

2231
01:31:26.510 --> 01:31:31.030
and all the kind of lifestyle stuff and that

2232
01:31:31.030 --> 01:31:33.270
'cause that's almost like a second book

2233
01:31:33.270 --> 01:31:34.760
and just make it a pure memoir

2234
01:31:34.760 --> 01:31:36.930
as opposed to this hybrid memoir

2235
01:31:36.930 --> 01:31:41.440
kind of lifestyle guide aspect that it has to it,

2236
01:31:41.440 --> 01:31:42.857
which I think is helpful to a lot of people--

2237
01:31:42.857 --> 01:31:44.240
But that might have got the,

2238
01:31:44.240 --> 01:31:46.371
that got people interested in,

2239
01:31:46.371 --> 01:31:47.580
and that probably helped you sell it.

2240
01:31:47.580 --> 01:31:49.750
But maybe it should've been, maybe, maybe.

2241
01:31:49.750 --> 01:31:52.240
But maybe that should've been a second book.

2242
01:31:52.240 --> 01:31:53.970
Maybe the title isn't great

2243
01:31:53.970 --> 01:31:57.020
and maybe I shouldn't be running on the cover.

2244
01:31:57.020 --> 01:31:58.032
No.

2245
01:31:58.032 --> 01:31:59.080
There seems to be some--
Come on.

2246
01:31:59.080 --> 01:32:00.610
Some conflicting opinions about that.

2247
01:32:00.610 --> 01:32:02.590
But I think when, I think it suffered from the fact

2248
01:32:02.590 --> 01:32:06.420
that when it came out with its title and the title image

2249
01:32:06.420 --> 01:32:08.970
that people thought it was a book about running,

2250
01:32:08.970 --> 01:32:10.777
which it kinda is but it really isn't.

2251
01:32:10.777 --> 01:32:11.610
No, right.

2252
01:32:11.610 --> 01:32:14.240
So I don't know that it really sells

2253
01:32:14.240 --> 01:32:16.340
the crux of what the book is about

2254
01:32:16.340 --> 01:32:18.730
and perhaps that was a barrier that prevented it

2255
01:32:18.730 --> 01:32:21.943
from breaking out a little bit more broadly.

2256
01:32:23.162 --> 01:32:25.720
At the same time like, I don't know.

2257
01:32:25.720 --> 01:32:26.823
I think I would,

2258
01:32:27.820 --> 01:32:29.730
I mean, I think I have a better grasp on the story.

2259
01:32:29.730 --> 01:32:31.780
And with some maturity, I have a better understanding

2260
01:32:31.780 --> 01:32:33.110
of some of the things that I went through

2261
01:32:33.110 --> 01:32:36.990
and I could like write to that a little bit more eloquently

2262
01:32:36.990 --> 01:32:40.006
and maturely than I did at the time.

2263
01:32:40.006 --> 01:32:40.839
Yeah, right.

2264
01:32:40.839 --> 01:32:43.350
'Cause distance always creates that.

2265
01:32:43.350 --> 01:32:45.480
I wouldn't change it whole cloth,

2266
01:32:45.480 --> 01:32:48.700
but I think I would take out any, like the first time,

2267
01:32:48.700 --> 01:32:50.590
the first edition of the book that came out,

2268
01:32:50.590 --> 01:32:53.560
I had like, "Here, you can find my protein powder.

2269
01:32:53.560 --> 01:32:54.950
Here," like stuff like that.

2270
01:32:54.950 --> 01:32:58.160
I was like, "I can't believe I put that in the book."

2271
01:32:58.160 --> 01:33:00.817
Like, "That had no place in the book."

2272
01:33:01.770 --> 01:33:04.060
Especially if you want to write something

2273
01:33:04.060 --> 01:33:05.573
that's gonna stand the test of time,

2274
01:33:05.573 --> 01:33:08.350
like get rid of all that nonsense

2275
01:33:08.350 --> 01:33:09.863
and just write a great story.

2276
01:33:11.240 --> 01:33:16.240
What about any plans for a future book by Mr. Rich Roll

2277
01:33:16.560 --> 01:33:17.393
through the publishers?

2278
01:33:17.393 --> 01:33:19.938
I know you're putting out these great books.

2279
01:33:19.938 --> 01:33:21.507
Yeah, I really great books do wanna write another book

2280
01:33:21.507 --> 01:33:23.890
and I definitely have another book in me.

2281
01:33:23.890 --> 01:33:26.890
The challenge is my life is so busy and full.

2282
01:33:26.890 --> 01:33:29.750
Like when I wrote "Finding Ultra", I had nothing going on.

2283
01:33:29.750 --> 01:33:31.250
I was, like I'm writing this book,

2284
01:33:31.250 --> 01:33:33.020
and I would just write it all day.

2285
01:33:33.020 --> 01:33:38.020
Now, like I'm occupied all day long, every single day.

2286
01:33:38.130 --> 01:33:40.400
I can't imagine being able to carve out time

2287
01:33:40.400 --> 01:33:41.233
to write a book.

2288
01:33:41.233 --> 01:33:43.480
I don't know how people with busy lives do that,

2289
01:33:43.480 --> 01:33:47.410
like there's no way it's gonna happen without help.

2290
01:33:47.410 --> 01:33:49.379
That's where the ghostwriters come in.

2291
01:33:49.379 --> 01:33:50.212
I know, I know.

2292
01:33:50.212 --> 01:33:51.807
But then I'm not a big fan of this--

2293
01:33:51.807 --> 01:33:53.450
I'm gonna have to work with,

2294
01:33:53.450 --> 01:33:54.810
but then it's the control thing.

2295
01:33:54.810 --> 01:33:55.960
It's like, "I'm a writer,"

2296
01:33:55.960 --> 01:33:58.720
like, "Why would I have somebody else help me write a book?"

2297
01:33:58.720 --> 01:34:02.110
But the reality is, yes, you may be,

2298
01:34:02.110 --> 01:34:05.510
consider yourself a writer, but like without,

2299
